From bf4eda8784e2a332b88267edcc38022fddedb0e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neil Kainga <t-neilkainga@microsoft.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:49:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] S4: cross-compile and link nnn for native Windows ARM64

Adds a Win32 portability layer so nnn -- which has no native Windows
build at all -- compiles and links for aarch64-w64-mingw32, producing a
self-contained ARM64 nnn.exe.

src/win/win_compat.{c,h} (new, ~1800 lines) implements the POSIX surface
mingw lacks, over Win32:
  - stat/lstat/fstatat via CreateFileW + GetFileInformationByHandle
  - dirent via FindFirstFileExW, populating d_type
  - statvfs via GetDiskFreeSpaceExW
  - realpath/readlink via GetFinalPathNameByHandleW
  - process creation via CreateProcessW with CommandLineToArgvW quoting
  - sigaction via SetConsoleCtrlHandler
  - directory change notification via ReadDirectoryChangesW, mirroring
    the existing HAIKU_NM API one-for-one
  - wcwidth/wcswidth, memmem, getline, strsep, strcasestr, ffs, link,
    fchmod, localtime_r, pipe

nnn.c changes are additive guards only; every POSIX branch is preserved
under #ifndef _WIN32, and the default POSIX build is byte-identical to
before (162,304 B, zero warnings).

The main structural change is the process model: Windows has no fork(),
so the fork/exec/wait triad in spawn(), get_output() and
buffer_command_output() is replaced by CreateProcessW calls that set up
stdio redirection before process creation rather than in a forked child.

Deferred to S5 and marked TODO(arm64): WIN_NM notification wiring,
the plugin control channel (needs a named pipe, not a FIFO), preview
pane streaming, and chmod-to-ACL mapping.

Verified: llvm-readobj reports IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_ARM64 (0xAA64);
imports are Windows system DLLs only, no vendored x64 binaries.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
